<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Vencemos started.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Vencemos started.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Caspian Securities analyst Paul Rodrguez started coverage of Venezuela's Corporacin Venezolana de Cementos SACA, or Vencemos, with a rating of buy.</p>
<p>-- &quot;Vencemos is among the cheapest cement stocks in Latin America on a cash flow valuation basis,&quot; he wrote in a report.  </p>
<p>-- He set a 1997 year-end price target on the series 1 stock of 1,895 bolivars, or $3.85, a share, &quot;representing a nominal bolivar return of 21 percent and a U.S. dollar return of 16 percent.&quot;</p>
<p>-- In Caracas, the series 1 shares were up 20 bolivars at 1,640 bolivars. The series 2 stock was up 60 bolivars to 1,560 bolivars.</p>
<p>((-- Ian Simpson, Wall Street desk, 212 859-1879))</p>
